# Derived by hand from Semantics ch. 8 ("Elements and the element statement": `@Element e` is the element statement at the same path, each taking the next number; a widget application is transparent; a `$` field is live, so the place changes in place) and Type System ch. 2 (an element is a plain value until a statement or a host places it): the passed button's label follows `$n` in the tick of the click, and its clicks are `!go`'s.
test a_passed_element_is_placed

tick 0
  added:
    0: Ui.Button(label="inc")
    1: Ui.Label(text="frame")
    2: Ui.Button(label="go 0")
    3: Ui.Button(label="more!")
    4: Ui.Label(text="went 0, shouts 0")

tick 1
  in:
    0: click
  changed:
    2: Ui.Button(label="go 1")

tick 2
  in:
    2: click
  changed:
    4: Ui.Label(text="went 1, shouts 0")

tick 3
  in:
    3: click
  changed:
    4: Ui.Label(text="went 1, shouts 1")
